1
00:00:00,583 --> 00:00:01,376
Jao!

2
00:00:01,418 --> 00:00:02,001
What?

3
00:00:02,043 --> 00:00:03,628
[KARA] I just wanted to tell you,

4
00:00:03,670 --> 00:00:05,462
wherever life takes you,

5
00:00:05,463 --> 00:00:06,797
never forget

6
00:00:06,798 --> 00:00:08,091
you’re a Siargaonon.

7
00:00:08,258 --> 00:00:09,968
And you’ll always have a home here.

8
00:00:13,179 --> 00:00:14,973
[QUINITO] Pearl, can we talk?

9
00:00:15,181 --> 00:00:17,475
I’ve been meaning to tell you this, just to make it clear.

10
00:00:17,517 --> 00:00:18,518
I like you a lot.

11
00:00:18,685 --> 00:00:21,187
And just so there’s no confusion, I’d like to date you.

12
00:00:21,479 --> 00:00:23,982
I’m just not ready to date anyone.

13
00:00:24,023 --> 00:00:25,108
[ARIEL] Han Bin oppa!

14
00:00:25,150 --> 00:00:26,567
Look. What’s the meaning of this?

15
00:00:26,568 --> 00:00:27,652
[HAN BIN] If you don’t mind,

16
00:00:27,694 --> 00:00:29,111
you can edit me out of the video.

17
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:30,905
- What? - Are you hiding something from us?

18
00:00:31,448 --> 00:00:33,241
Jao’s in Cebu.

19
00:00:33,283 --> 00:00:34,868
[CAROL] Just admit it already!

20
00:00:34,909 --> 00:00:36,994
- You miss him! - I don’t!

21
00:00:36,995 --> 00:00:39,164
Every time I say Jao’s name,

22
00:00:39,205 --> 00:00:40,415
you smile.

23
00:00:40,623 --> 00:00:41,750
[CAROL] See?

24
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:43,209
Ice candy!

25
00:00:43,251 --> 00:00:44,419
Would you like an ice candy?

26
00:00:44,461 --> 00:00:45,669
Coconut or mango?

27
00:00:45,670 --> 00:00:46,087
Boat.

28
00:00:46,129 --> 00:00:46,713
Boat?

29
00:00:46,755 --> 00:00:47,714
Never mind. I just…

30
00:00:47,756 --> 00:00:48,757
suddenly missed someone.

31
00:00:48,798 --> 00:00:49,798
[JAO] Yes, sir?

32
00:00:49,799 --> 00:00:51,425
You told me to take a vacation.

33
00:00:51,426 --> 00:00:52,135
I’m good.

34
00:00:52,136 --> 00:00:53,344
[PAUL ON THE PHONE] So, where are you?

35
00:00:53,386 --> 00:00:54,471
Where I should be.

36
00:00:55,096 --> 00:00:56,097
[JAO] Hi, miss.

37
00:01:07,609 --> 00:01:08,818
Who are you calling “miss”?

38
00:01:10,320 --> 00:01:11,320
I missed you, too.

39
00:01:11,321 --> 00:01:12,530
[KARA SCOFFS]

40
00:01:13,740 --> 00:01:14,824
Okay.

41
00:01:15,450 --> 00:01:16,743
Why? Did I say something wrong?

42
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:19,537
I thought you were in Cebu?

43
00:01:20,038 --> 00:01:22,415
Paul told me to...

44
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:25,460
take three weeks off.

45
00:01:26,920 --> 00:01:27,921
Wait…

46
00:01:28,213 --> 00:01:29,214
How did you know?

47
00:01:30,089 --> 00:01:31,674
Tantan told us.

48
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:37,055
Well, he told me to take three weeks off, but...

49
00:01:37,514 --> 00:01:39,224
Cebu just wasn’t my vibe.

50
00:01:40,350 --> 00:01:41,351
Why not?

51
00:01:41,601 --> 00:01:43,435
- Cebu is beautiful. - Yeah.

52
00:01:43,436 --> 00:01:45,730
It’s beautiful and the food is good.

53
00:01:46,940 --> 00:01:48,358
But it’s not Siargao.

54
00:01:49,442 --> 00:01:50,860
And you're not there.

55
00:01:56,991 --> 00:01:58,201
Got any plans tomorrow?

56
00:01:58,368 --> 00:01:59,369
Nope.

57
00:02:00,578 --> 00:02:01,579
Good.

58
00:02:27,063 --> 00:02:31,568
[ALON BY JL]

59
00:04:02,075 --> 00:04:03,159
[JAO] Can I ask you something?

60
00:04:05,370 --> 00:04:06,371
[KARA] What?

61
00:04:07,455 --> 00:04:09,040
[JAO] Why are you so guarded?

62
00:04:09,749 --> 00:04:11,583
[JAO] I’ve felt that from the start.

63
00:04:11,584 --> 00:04:14,671
No matter how warm and welcoming you are to others,

64
00:04:15,296 --> 00:04:17,215
it always feels like there’s a wall I have to break through

65
00:04:17,257 --> 00:04:18,841
to really get to know you.

66
00:04:22,178 --> 00:04:23,304
[KARA] Really?

67
00:04:24,097 --> 00:04:26,557
Sorry if I made you feel that way.

68
00:04:27,350 --> 00:04:29,519
I guess it’s not deliberate.

69
00:04:30,269 --> 00:04:34,774
I’ve just been badly hurt in the past.

70
00:04:34,899 --> 00:04:36,526
So maybe I'm just being careful.

71
00:04:39,112 --> 00:04:40,238
[JAO] With me?

72
00:04:42,031 --> 00:04:43,533
[KARA] Not just with you.

73
00:04:44,200 --> 00:04:46,326
Maybe in general.

74
00:04:46,327 --> 00:04:49,122
About the people I let into my life...

75
00:04:49,831 --> 00:04:53,042
The people I choose to trust...

76
00:04:53,126 --> 00:04:54,627
The people I could love.

77
00:04:56,212 --> 00:04:57,422
[JAO] Kara,

78
00:04:57,547 --> 00:04:59,632
I still want to get to know you better.

79
00:05:00,550 --> 00:05:02,552
Can you give me a chance?

80
00:05:04,012 --> 00:05:05,513
[KARA] You can try.

81
00:05:06,264 --> 00:05:07,890
But before you get to know me,

82
00:05:08,224 --> 00:05:10,560
I think it’s time you meet Ruth.

83
00:05:19,610 --> 00:05:21,529
Why did you buy me a burger?

84
00:05:21,946 --> 00:05:23,448
Because you’re my friend.

85
00:05:23,489 --> 00:05:24,449
Aw…

86
00:05:24,490 --> 00:05:25,992
I’m not falling for that.

87
00:05:26,868 --> 00:05:29,662
Are you here to accuse me of more crazy things?

88
00:05:29,996 --> 00:05:30,997
Like what?

89
00:05:31,164 --> 00:05:32,164
Like…

90
00:05:32,165 --> 00:05:33,166
I don’t know!

91
00:05:33,207 --> 00:05:35,125
Like, I’m a yoga teacher in India,

92
00:05:35,126 --> 00:05:37,544
who can’t pronounce “namaste” correctly.

93
00:05:37,545 --> 00:05:39,671
- Or... - Or you’re a Korean oppa…

94
00:05:39,672 --> 00:05:41,548
who travels all around Asia

95
00:05:41,549 --> 00:05:43,342
and falls in love with the Philippines,

96
00:05:43,593 --> 00:05:45,261
falls in love with the island of Siargao,

97
00:05:45,303 --> 00:05:47,721
and falls in love with my beautiful sister,

98
00:05:47,722 --> 00:05:48,723
Pearl.

99
00:05:54,562 --> 00:05:55,563
It’s okay!

100
00:05:55,897 --> 00:05:57,065
I like you for Pearl.

101
00:05:58,608 --> 00:06:00,234
I don’t know what you’re talking about.

102
00:06:01,819 --> 00:06:02,820
Hey.

103
00:06:03,821 --> 00:06:04,489
It’s okay.

104
00:06:04,530 --> 00:06:06,532
I like you for Pearl. I know you will be good for her.

105
00:06:09,202 --> 00:06:10,203
Really?

106
00:06:10,244 --> 00:06:11,245
[ARIEL] Really!

107
00:06:11,454 --> 00:06:12,455
[SIARGAONON] Really.

108
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:14,874
I know you’ll be good for her.

109
00:06:20,004 --> 00:06:21,005
But I think…

110
00:06:22,215 --> 00:06:25,218
Pearl wants to explore and experience the world.

111
00:06:25,551 --> 00:06:27,261
Yeah, good for her.

112
00:06:27,678 --> 00:06:28,262
But...

113
00:06:28,554 --> 00:06:29,764
bad for me.

114
00:06:31,140 --> 00:06:33,184
And I don’t think she likes me.

115
00:06:34,602 --> 00:06:35,812
Han Bin oppa…

116
00:06:36,938 --> 00:06:38,314
I know my sister.

117
00:06:40,358 --> 00:06:42,110
I feel like she likes you.

118
00:06:42,610 --> 00:06:44,654
[ARIEL] But she doesn’t realize it yet.

119
00:06:45,029 --> 00:06:47,240
You know why? Because…

120
00:06:47,698 --> 00:06:48,699
it’s your fault.

121
00:06:48,825 --> 00:06:50,743
It’s because you don’t express your true feelings,

122
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,453
you’re always so serious around her.

123
00:06:53,704 --> 00:06:54,704
But...

124
00:06:54,705 --> 00:06:56,707
Pearl may not say much about it to me,

125
00:06:57,208 --> 00:06:58,209
but I can tell

126
00:06:58,251 --> 00:07:01,546
she’s dreaming of a life beyond this paradise.

127
00:07:03,297 --> 00:07:04,590
I’ll tell you a story.

128
00:07:05,174 --> 00:07:06,467
Our mother said that

129
00:07:06,843 --> 00:07:09,137
when Pearl was five years old,

130
00:07:09,679 --> 00:07:11,389
she met this Greek woman,

131
00:07:11,597 --> 00:07:13,224
who was visiting the island.

132
00:07:13,474 --> 00:07:15,476
And this Greek woman told Pearl

133
00:07:15,518 --> 00:07:17,895
that she can taste all flavors of ice cream

134
00:07:17,937 --> 00:07:20,314
and all kinds of chocolate in Europe.

135
00:07:20,940 --> 00:07:23,234
And that’s when she started becoming curious.

136
00:07:24,068 --> 00:07:25,194
Shallow, right?

137
00:07:25,361 --> 00:07:26,154
No!

138
00:07:26,155 --> 00:07:27,363
Not at all shallow.

139
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:30,950
Some childhood memories really stay with you.

140
00:07:31,242 --> 00:07:34,036
And some memories even shape our future.

141
00:07:34,787 --> 00:07:36,497
Hm. Says who?

142
00:07:36,998 --> 00:07:39,083
Says a psychologist from…

143
00:07:39,125 --> 00:07:40,126
Norway?

144
00:07:40,710 --> 00:07:41,711
Says me.

145
00:07:41,878 --> 00:07:43,670
A young boy from Seoul,

146
00:07:43,671 --> 00:07:45,673
who dreamed of seeing the world

147
00:07:45,923 --> 00:07:49,427
because my sister destroyed the globe my father gave me.

148
00:07:51,721 --> 00:07:52,722
[HAN BIN SIGHS]

149
00:07:53,598 --> 00:07:54,599
Pearl…

150
00:07:56,392 --> 00:07:57,894
is just like me.

151
00:08:00,396 --> 00:08:02,481
Chocolate and ice cream

152
00:08:02,899 --> 00:08:04,901
represent a bigger world for her.

153
00:08:05,026 --> 00:08:06,527
She must be smart.

154
00:08:07,361 --> 00:08:08,654
She’s very smart.

155
00:08:10,031 --> 00:08:11,991
Always so imaginative and

156
00:08:12,033 --> 00:08:15,536
curious and asks so many questions.

157
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:18,956
So…

158
00:08:19,207 --> 00:08:20,208
what should I do?

159
00:08:20,541 --> 00:08:22,752
You know, Quinito is already close to her.

160
00:08:23,127 --> 00:08:24,252
[ARIEL] You know why?

161
00:08:24,253 --> 00:08:26,756
Because Quinito says what he feels.

162
00:08:26,797 --> 00:08:28,506
He’s expressive, he’s proactive...

163
00:08:28,507 --> 00:08:29,508
unlike you!

164
00:08:30,176 --> 00:08:31,969
[HAN BIN] Then what do you want me to do?

165
00:08:33,137 --> 00:08:35,056
Dance like Quinito like this?

166
00:08:35,514 --> 00:08:36,682
- [ARIEL] Yeah! - Huh?

167
00:08:36,724 --> 00:08:38,017
[SIARGAONON] You got the beat!

168
00:08:38,059 --> 00:08:39,851
[SINGS IN SIARGAONON] You got the beat!

169
00:08:39,852 --> 00:08:40,977
Yeah, you should dance like that.

170
00:08:40,978 --> 00:08:42,395
- We’ll practice later. - [HAN BIN LAUGHS]

171
00:08:42,396 --> 00:08:43,814
I’ll teach you.

172
00:08:44,315 --> 00:08:45,440
Or do the aegyo.

173
00:08:45,441 --> 00:08:46,691
Um, aegyo?

174
00:08:46,692 --> 00:08:48,402
- [ARIEL] Yeah, aegyo! - Like how?

175
00:08:58,412 --> 00:08:59,412
[JAO] Are these the mangroves?

176
00:08:59,413 --> 00:09:00,206
[KARA] Yeah.

177
00:09:01,499 --> 00:09:03,334
Ruth, Jao.

178
00:09:03,376 --> 00:09:04,961
Jao, this is Ruth.

179
00:09:05,962 --> 00:09:08,296
Ruth as in...

180
00:09:08,297 --> 00:09:09,507
R-O-O-T?

181
00:09:09,966 --> 00:09:11,050
As in “root”? Or…

182
00:09:11,092 --> 00:09:13,469
Ruth as in R-U-T-H?

183
00:09:14,011 --> 00:09:15,096
As in the name?

184
00:09:15,972 --> 00:09:16,681
Boat!

185
00:09:16,722 --> 00:09:18,723
[KARA AND JAO LAUGH]

186
00:09:18,724 --> 00:09:20,226
Hi, Ruth! Nice to meet you.

187
00:09:20,268 --> 00:09:21,352
I’m Jao.

188
00:09:21,686 --> 00:09:23,688
I planted Ruth myself.

189
00:09:23,980 --> 00:09:26,857
The mangroves helped a lot during Typhoon Odette.

190
00:09:27,733 --> 00:09:31,320
They protected so many homes from the storm surge.

191
00:09:31,487 --> 00:09:33,906
Ruth and all her kind are strong and resilient.

192
00:09:35,324 --> 00:09:39,120
Mangroves really are essential to protecting Siargao, huh?

193
00:09:39,161 --> 00:09:40,162
Yeah.

194
00:09:41,414 --> 00:09:42,832
That’s why I hope…

195
00:09:42,873 --> 00:09:45,376
there’ll be more mangroves across the Philippines.

196
00:09:49,338 --> 00:09:52,341
Now that you’ve met Ruth,

197
00:09:52,925 --> 00:09:54,927
you have to make her a promise.

198
00:09:55,469 --> 00:09:56,554
Promise what?

199
00:09:57,096 --> 00:09:59,097
Promise that...

200
00:09:59,098 --> 00:10:00,808
you’ll protect her

201
00:10:01,142 --> 00:10:03,436
and all her fellow mangroves.

202
00:10:06,397 --> 00:10:07,398
Okay.

203
00:10:08,607 --> 00:10:10,609
So, from this day,

204
00:10:11,068 --> 00:10:13,778
I promise to help you

205
00:10:13,779 --> 00:10:15,197
protect Ruth

206
00:10:15,823 --> 00:10:18,326
and every mangrove here in Siargao.

207
00:10:18,868 --> 00:10:20,870
Did you hear that Ruth?

208
00:10:22,872 --> 00:10:24,081
She said thanks.

209
00:10:25,041 --> 00:10:25,666
She did?

210
00:10:25,708 --> 00:10:27,376
[KARA AND JAO CHUCKLE]

211
00:10:28,753 --> 00:10:30,963
Ruth knows everything about me.

212
00:10:31,922 --> 00:10:34,215
I whisper to her all my doubts,

213
00:10:34,216 --> 00:10:36,635
fears, secrets.

214
00:10:37,595 --> 00:10:38,596
Everything.

215
00:10:39,805 --> 00:10:41,307
You should try talking to her, too.

216
00:10:42,683 --> 00:10:43,893
What do I say?

217
00:10:43,934 --> 00:10:45,895
[KARA] Anything! Tell her your secrets.

218
00:10:46,228 --> 00:10:46,937
Huh?

219
00:10:47,021 --> 00:10:47,855
Already?

220
00:10:48,189 --> 00:10:49,273
Yes!

221
00:10:49,315 --> 00:10:51,400
- I won’t listen. - Okay, okay.

222
00:10:57,365 --> 00:11:05,873
[JAO WHISPERS INAUDIBLY]

223
00:11:09,126 --> 00:11:10,127
[JAO] Okay.

224
00:11:12,505 --> 00:11:14,173
Ruth is saying something, Kara.

225
00:11:15,841 --> 00:11:16,509
Uh...

226
00:11:16,550 --> 00:11:17,551
Okay.

227
00:11:19,345 --> 00:11:21,764
She said I should tell you myself.

228
00:11:23,474 --> 00:11:24,475
What is it?

229
00:11:30,731 --> 00:11:32,733
I want more than friendship, Kara.

230
00:11:40,324 --> 00:11:41,492
I want us to...

231
00:11:41,909 --> 00:11:43,702
be more than what we are right now.

232
00:11:46,789 --> 00:11:48,833
I want to get to know you more.

233
00:11:49,333 --> 00:11:50,543
All of you.

234
00:11:51,794 --> 00:11:53,421
Not to pressure you but…

235
00:11:54,255 --> 00:11:56,382
to make you feel that you’re safe with me.

236
00:11:59,176 --> 00:12:00,177
So,

237
00:12:01,595 --> 00:12:02,805
if you’ll let me,

238
00:12:04,807 --> 00:12:06,183
please let me in?

239
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:10,479
Jao, I’m hard to love.

240
00:12:10,521 --> 00:12:12,523
Then why does this feel so easy?

241
00:12:18,988 --> 00:12:19,989
I’m scared.

242
00:12:21,574 --> 00:12:23,576
I fall too deeply.

243
00:12:25,619 --> 00:12:27,997
I’m afraid the next time it happens, I’ll drown.

244
00:12:28,038 --> 00:12:29,123
No, no, no…

245
00:12:32,835 --> 00:12:34,795
Kara, we won’t rush anything.

246
00:12:36,088 --> 00:12:38,090
Like what you said before…

247
00:12:39,508 --> 00:12:41,802
"Just go with the flow and ride the waves."

248
00:12:42,219 --> 00:12:43,929
I’ll ride it with you, Kara.

249
00:12:44,763 --> 00:12:46,182
I’ll ride the waves with you.

250
00:12:47,683 --> 00:12:49,268
And now that I’m here,

251
00:12:50,978 --> 00:12:52,980
I won’t let you drown.

252
00:13:08,162 --> 00:13:09,163
[HAN BIN] Hello!

253
00:13:09,205 --> 00:13:10,289
- Hi! - Hi!

254
00:13:10,623 --> 00:13:12,500
We have a reservation for two nights.

255
00:13:12,541 --> 00:13:15,127
Okay, may I ask for the reservation name, please?

256
00:13:15,169 --> 00:13:16,669
Yeah, it’s Ava Brooks.

257
00:13:16,670 --> 00:13:17,671
Okay.

258
00:13:18,839 --> 00:13:20,674
All right, I got it.

259
00:13:22,259 --> 00:13:24,553
You know, you look like a K-pop star.

260
00:13:25,054 --> 00:13:25,888
Me?

261
00:13:26,180 --> 00:13:27,305
Um…

262
00:13:27,306 --> 00:13:29,099
actually, I’ve heard that before,

263
00:13:29,141 --> 00:13:30,558
but no.

264
00:13:30,559 --> 00:13:31,852
It’s just the island air.

265
00:13:31,894 --> 00:13:33,771
And you have a great smile.

266
00:13:33,812 --> 00:13:35,813
- Yeah, it’s so white. - [HAN BIN CHUCKLES]

267
00:13:35,814 --> 00:13:37,233
[GUEST] It’s so refreshing.

268
00:13:38,442 --> 00:13:39,443
Thank you.

269
00:13:39,944 --> 00:13:41,946
Okay. Um...

270
00:13:42,821 --> 00:13:44,031
[HAN BIN] Uh...

271
00:13:44,073 --> 00:13:45,074
Yes!

272
00:13:46,825 --> 00:13:48,410
- Here we go. - Thank you.

273
00:13:48,911 --> 00:13:51,205
Wait, is that your secret?

274
00:13:52,289 --> 00:13:55,208
Yeah, actually, it’s kind of my secret.

275
00:13:55,209 --> 00:13:57,711
It’s for maximum confidence.

276
00:13:57,753 --> 00:13:59,338
Well, it’s working.

277
00:13:59,922 --> 00:14:01,924
Are you single or taken?

278
00:14:02,132 --> 00:14:03,132
Um...

279
00:14:03,133 --> 00:14:04,259
I’m single

280
00:14:04,260 --> 00:14:06,053
but my heart is already taken.

281
00:14:06,095 --> 00:14:07,096
Aw!

282
00:14:07,137 --> 00:14:08,305
She’s a lucky girl.

283
00:14:08,347 --> 00:14:09,932
[HAN BIN CHUCKLES]

284
00:14:09,974 --> 00:14:10,974
Okay.

285
00:14:10,975 --> 00:14:11,976
So...

286
00:14:12,393 --> 00:14:14,103
enjoy your stay.

287
00:14:14,144 --> 00:14:14,812
Thank you!

288
00:14:14,853 --> 00:14:16,271
[SIARGAONON] Thank you!

289
00:14:16,272 --> 00:14:17,982
- [GUESTS] Thank you! - Thank you, guys!

290
00:14:46,552 --> 00:14:48,846
[KARA] The key to good surfing is timing.

291
00:14:51,765 --> 00:14:54,476
[JAO] You have to learn how to be one with the waves.

292
00:14:57,563 --> 00:14:59,188
[KARA] If you get the timing right,

293
00:14:59,189 --> 00:15:00,691
you can ride a good wave.

294
00:15:15,956 --> 00:15:19,084
[JAO] But if you rush, you may not catch it.

295
00:15:19,376 --> 00:15:20,793
You'll miss the wave...

296
00:15:20,794 --> 00:15:22,796
and falling hurts.

297
00:15:27,176 --> 00:15:29,511
[KARA] Is it the same as falling in love?

298
00:15:29,637 --> 00:15:30,846
[JAO] Sometimes.

299
00:15:33,140 --> 00:15:35,142
[JAO] But you have to take the risk.

300
00:15:37,019 --> 00:15:38,311
Because when you get the chance

301
00:15:38,312 --> 00:15:40,022
to ride out a good relationship,

302
00:15:40,648 --> 00:15:42,650
it’s the best feeling in the world.

303
00:15:46,320 --> 00:15:48,197
[JAO] I’m way rusty.

304
00:15:48,238 --> 00:15:49,238
[KARA] Not at all!

305
00:15:49,263 --> 00:15:50,263
But you know,

306
00:15:50,288 --> 00:15:52,206
just give yourself more time back on the board,

307
00:15:52,231 --> 00:15:53,608
and it’ll all come back to you.

308
00:15:54,444 --> 00:15:56,744
[JAO] I really missed the waves in Siargao.

309
00:15:57,770 --> 00:15:58,770
Maybe...

310
00:15:58,897 --> 00:15:59,898
Uh...

311
00:15:59,958 --> 00:16:01,085
I just need to keep surfing.

312
00:16:01,110 --> 00:16:04,113
I’m sure I’ll get the feel for it again.

313
00:16:05,339 --> 00:16:06,340
[WOMAN] Jao!

314
00:16:35,202 --> 00:16:36,412
You know,

315
00:16:36,453 --> 00:16:38,414
you two are more like people trying to make it work

316
00:16:38,455 --> 00:16:40,457
than two people who naturally fit.

317
00:16:41,375 --> 00:16:42,751
[HAN BIN] Jao! Join us.

318
00:16:43,168 --> 00:16:44,545
[QUINITO] At least Jao...

319
00:16:44,586 --> 00:16:46,588
always seems happy with Kara.

320
00:16:46,630 --> 00:16:48,090
I’m just a happy guy.

321
00:16:48,132 --> 00:16:49,549
What’s going on between you two?

322
00:16:49,550 --> 00:16:51,552
You like Kara, don’t you?

323
00:16:51,593 --> 00:16:52,761
Uh…

324
00:16:52,803 --> 00:16:55,513
we just like spending a lot of time together.

325
00:16:55,514 --> 00:16:57,516
- He’s blushing! - [HAN BIN] Look at him!

326
00:16:57,558 --> 00:16:59,058
[QUINITO AND HAN BIN LAUGH]

327
00:16:59,059 --> 00:16:59,893
[ARCHIE] Hi, Kara.

328
00:16:59,894 --> 00:17:01,103
[KARA] Archie!

329
00:17:01,145 --> 00:17:02,521
Long time!

330
00:17:02,563 --> 00:17:04,148
When did you get back?

331
00:17:04,189 --> 00:17:06,190
- [ARCHIE] I’ve missed you. - [KARA] I’ve missed you, too!

332
00:17:06,191 --> 00:17:07,608
Jao, this is Archie.

333
00:17:07,609 --> 00:17:08,943
Archie, this is Jao.

334
00:17:08,944 --> 00:17:09,945
I’m Jao.

335
00:17:09,987 --> 00:17:11,071
What do you do?

336
00:17:11,113 --> 00:17:12,405
Uh… I’m on vacation,

337
00:17:12,406 --> 00:17:14,825
so I’m not really interested to talk about work.
